(d) enquire into the bona fide of an arrest whenever
a person is detained without a warrant. If he
considers the arrest unlawful or the evidence does
not justify the charge, he shall not accept the
prisoner but—
(i) allow the person to leave;
(ii) record the action taken in the Station
Diary;
(iii) inform the First Division Officer-in-charge
of the area of the action he took as soon as
possible.
(e) supervise the processing of the prisoner and ensure
that the correct charge is laid;
(f) ensure that the arrested person is informed of—
(i) his rights to retain and instruct without
delay a legal adviser of his own choice;
(ii) his rights to hold communication with his
legal adviser;
(iii) his entitlement to a telephone call to his
legal adviser, family or friend;
(iv) the person in custody is treated in accor-
dance with the requirements of Part II of
S.O. 32.
(g) ensure that entries with respect to the actions
taken at paragraph 7 (f) are recorded in the Station
Diary;
(h) ensure that all the duties assigned to the
Charge Room and Compound Sentries are effectively
carried out;
(i) issue of arms and ammunition and their retrieval;
(j) detail police officers to investigate reports;
(k) submit immediately to the Officer in charge of the
Division, an extract of any report made by a member
of the public against police officers;
(l) ensure the preparation and submission of
morning reports;
