(c) answer the telephone in accordance with
instructions as set out in Standing Order 39;
(d) record the telephone messages and wireless
communications inclusive of telephone tolls in the
register;
(e) send telephone messages and transmit wireless
communications;
(f) keep the wireless communications on at all times;
(g) inform the Second Division Officer-in-charge
of the Charge Room of all serious reports and
occurrences;
(h) classify the reports and record them in the relevant
registers;
(i) assist in the processing of prisoners, e.g., searching
and fingerprinting;
(j) visit cells once every hour or as directed and record
such visit immediately thereafter in the Station
Diary;
(k) process applications for Certificates of Character;
(l) hoist and lower flags at Station;
(m) report any breaches of discipline to his immediate
senior in rank;
(n) perform any other duties as may be assigned to him
from time to time.
9. Whenever a First Division Officer or an Inspector arrives at
a Station—
(a) The first police officer recognising him shall call the
Charge Room to attention.
